{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pulls/33","id":4502145192,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT3jXmM8AAAABDFlIqA","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/33","diff_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/33.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/33.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/issues/33","number":33,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Integrate reproducible native ARM64 MSYS runtime and fault recovery","user":{"login":"crutkas","id":1462282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjIyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1462282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"## Summary\n\nIntegrates the recovered ARM64 runtime source, maintained build/reproducibility fixes, mechanical autoload/export closure, and the qualified ARM64 myfault repair into one source-built cohort. No prebuilt `sigfe.o` substitution.\n\n- Explicit configured `__MSYS__` personality, fail-closed `.word`/`.long` TLS generation, correct ARM64 source lists, resource include propagation, `LDFLAGS`, and durable actual link-command records.\n- Checked cygheap reservation/commit in both initialization paths, permanent stack/heap no-access gap, and accurate `child_copy` short-count/Win32 error diagnostics.\n- Exact mechanical sources from `846c26818`, real NetAPI/User32 libraries, retained execvp fixes from `7b711aada`, and ARM64 myfault context-copy/unwind-phase filtering from patch `970f1beb…`.\n- Permanent guard, jump-buffer, ucontext, environment, signal-register and internal EFAULT regressions.\n\n## Labelled progression\n\nThese counts describe different scopes and must not be summed or treated as interchangeable:\n\n| Stage | Result and scope |\n|---|---|\n| Inherited reported scaffold | 254/310 objects, 15 errors; historical report, not a new measurement here. |\n| Earlier conditional diagnostic | 271/310 with temporary fixes; not sealed product admission. |\n| Mechanical owner | 3 targeted objects, 431 autoload globals, 1763 exports; private DLL `27491fce…`, native random/env/fork smoke. |\n| Reproducibility/startup | Two independent 8-job runtime builds, 181 runtime archive members, 8 bit-identical artifacts; DLL `72c16960…`; 10 native core controls. |\n| Myfault integration | Two fresh full builds reproduced `5aa79930…`; same fault executable succeeds ordinary/debug/no-context. Failed copy-only and phase-only controls are preserved. |\n| **Final combined cohort** | **Two independent 12-job runtime builds match all 8 tracked artifacts. DLL `907afa099a69aa3c13d4e3b30eeba18c4a6b1766d5fa39b4746fae23c3f9e76c`.** Qualified newlib was reused, not rebuilt. |\n\n## Native evidence\n\n- 14 core/guard/jump/ucontext/ctype/math/ordinary-C++/signal/fault controls passed, including both unchanged peer probes and newly built permanent probes.\n- Strong signal probe: 16 deliveries preserving integer, all 32 full vector registers and control state.\n- The same internal fault executable recovered eight protected-page `uname` calls as EFAULT in ordinary, debugger and no-context debugger runs. Each debugger run forwarded eight real AV events as `DBG_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED`, performed zero memory/register writes, and joined the same PID/creation generation to raw exit 0.\n- Exact mechanical smoke preserved random reads, `env .` returning 126/Permission denied, and fork/wait exit 7. **Its semantic result passes, but the unchanged conservative observer retains raw child codes 32256 and 1792 as rejected high exits. No normalization or observer-pass override was added.**\n- Fresh normal compiler-link readiness verified ARM64 process identity and the actual combined DLL path.\n\n## Corrections and limits\n\nThe ARM64 trampoline implementation was not unwritten: the demonstrated zero-output failure selected stale x86-only generator `74f502` instead of recovered ARM64 `180d3e`. The native `61d9664a…` signal object was independent assembler/export evidence, not a replacement object.\n\nThe dated “12:24” DLL could not be located by any owner. Historical recipe `f6d85275…` / blob `86bca711…` is preserved, but its association with that DLL is explicitly **UNPROVEN**. It omits `winver.o` and hand-selects archive members; it is not the maintained build method. Forensics is closed as unresolvable by available evidence.\n\nThis is a coherent runtime/build qualification, not a full Git distribution, generic C++ debugger parity, or broad exit-domain admission. Old SDKs and failed cohorts remain immutable.\n\nRelated source landings: #32 and crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build#11. Peer source commits are attributed in the integration commit. The user authorized commit/push/PR to the `crutkas/*` forks on 2026-09-10; no upstream submission is requested.","created_at":"2026-09-11T03:08:22Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T03:08:22Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e19200e6684168247a03a015c80dd0d1e59a8e72","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pulls/33/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pulls/33/comments","review_comm